cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this harness, its fixtures or the pilot data, please cite it as below."
title: "Review Blind Spot: measuring shared misses in AI code review"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Review Blind Spot contributors"
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-11-10"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Venorium/review-blindspot"
keywords:
  - code review
  - LLM evaluation
  - AI agents
  - agent skills
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  An offline-first harness that measures when AI code-review protocols approve
  faulty changes or miss the same defects, kept separate from wrong-reason
  rejections, abstentions, technical failures and resource use. Includes an
  Agent Skill for Codex and Claude Code that keeps local reviews evidence-backed
  and flags stale conclusions, and an exploratory pilot with three open-weight
  models run locally through Ollama.
